    "The policy has deepened financial anxiety in the village, especially for those like me who must carefully manage every franc, as rising construction costs and potential tax increases threaten the stability of everyday life.",
    "Through conversations with Anna and Sandrine, I've learned that the community is divided: while some see the new school as a hopeful investment for the children, many others—especially those on tight budgets—fear it will only benefit the wealthy or construction companies at the expense of ordinary villagers.",
    "My initial hope that the school project might bring long-term good has faded into doubt and unease; the tangible burden of higher prices and taxes has made me question whether the policy truly serves the whole village or only a select few."
  ]
}

{
  "insights": [
    "The policy's tax increase weighs heavily on small businesses and modest households, including those of my students and colleagues, creating a tangible sense of financial strain that I must address to maintain their trust and support.",
    "Through conversations with Felix, Anna, and Therese, I've learned that while there is broad recognition of the school and daycare as vital economic levers for Linden's future, there is also deep-seated concern among local stakeholders—especially farmers like npc_03—about the disproportionate burden on those who sustain the community's basic needs.",
    "My conviction that investment in education is essential for Linden's long-term prosperity has grown stronger, but so has my awareness that this must be communicated with empathy and concrete reassurance about fiscal fairness, linking school improvements directly to local employment and commerce to bridge the gap between economic vision and personal hardship."
  ]
